{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A]Gentle [F#m]Mary [A]laid [D]her [E]child [D]lowly in a [A]manger;
[A]There He [F#m]lay, the [A]un[D]de[E]filed, [D]to the world a [A]stranger:
[A]Such [D]a [E]babe in [A]such [E]a [F#m]place, [D]can He be the [A]Savior?
[A]Ask the [D]saved of [F#m]all the [E]race [A]who [D]have [E]found His [F#m]fa__[D]__[A]vor.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[A]Angels [F#m]sang a[A]bout [D]His [E]birth; [D]wise men sought and [A]found Him;
[A]Heaven’s [F#m]star shone [A]bright[D]ly [E]forth, [D]glory all a[A]round Him:
[A]Shep[D]herds [E]saw the [A]won[E]drous [F#m]sight, [D]heard the angels [A]singing;
[A]All the [D]plains were [F#m]lit that [E]night, [A]all [D]the [E]hills were [F#m]ring__[D]__[A]ing.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[A]Gentle [F#m]Mary [A]laid [D]her [E]child [D]lowly in a [A]manger;
[A]He is [F#m]still the [A]un[D]de[E]filed, [D]but no more a [A]stranger:
[A]Son [D]of [E]God, of [A]hum[E]ble [F#m]birth, [D]beautiful the [A]story;
[A]Praise His [D]name in [F#m]all the [E]earth, [A]hail [D]the [E]King of [F#m]glo__[D]__[A]ry!
{end_of_verse}
